osd: lay the OSD out in the window's own pixels

mpv's OSD sets its margins through libass's style, whose MarginL and
MarginV are whole numbers in the track's PlayRes, and an OSD track's
PlayResY was always 288. A margin then lands in steps of the window's
height over 288, about 6 device pixels in a window 1747 tall, so no
setting can put a message's ink 24 logical pixels from the window's edge
at a scale of 2: the nearest are 23 and 26.

The OSD's PlayResY is now the window's height, where that is more than
288, so a margin or an outline lands on a whole device pixel. Nothing else
changes: mpv scales every OSD size, its font, outline, shadow, spacing and
margins, by PlayResY over 720, and libass draws them at the window's
height over PlayResY, so each is drawn as large as before. Tracks that
give their own PlayRes, as scripts' overlays and subtitles do, are
untouched.

--- a/sub/osd_libass.c
+++ b/sub/osd_libass.c
@@ -104,7 +104,9 @@
     if (vo_res->display_par > 0)
         aspect = aspect / vo_res->display_par;
 
-    track->PlayResY = ass->res_y ? ass->res_y : MP_ASS_FONT_PLAYRESY;
+    // In the window's pixels, so libass's whole-number margins land on one.
+    track->PlayResY = ass->res_y ? ass->res_y
+                                 : MPMAX(vo_res->h, MP_ASS_FONT_PLAYRESY);
     track->PlayResX = ass->res_x ? ass->res_x : track->PlayResY * aspect;
 
     // Force libass to clear its internal cache - it doesn't check for
